[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Petrov's Defense"]
[Variation "Petrov's Defense: Stafford Gambit Accepted"]
[ECO "C42"]
[Character "sharp"]
[Risk "high"]
[EarlyMate "black"]
[Tricks "trap,mate-threat"]
[Themes "f2-attack"]
[Refutes "1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nf6 3. Nxe5 Nc6?! 4. Nxc6 dxc6 5. Nc3"]
[For "white"]
[Kind "against-us"]
[Opponent "3...Nc6"]
[Start "stafford-gambit 4...dxc6"]

5. Nc3 $6 { A natural developing move, but it lets Black build the attack on f2 with tempo. 5.d3 is calmer and keeps everything protected. } 5... Bc5 { Aims the bishop at f2, which only the king guards. } 6. Bd3 $2 { Develops but leaves f2 weak, so ...Ng4 comes with force. The quiet 6.h3 stops the knight from reaching g4. } 6... Ng4 { Now f2 is attacked twice, and ...Qh4 will make it three. White cannot parry everything. } 7. f4 Qh4+ 8. g3 Qh3 9. Bf1 Bf2+ 10. Ke2 *
